1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,322
The lottery's information security director rigged the lottery in five states.

2
00:00:04,822 --> 00:00:07,409
His name is Eddie Tipton. So where did he work?

3
00:00:07,709 --> 00:00:10,208
At the Multi-State Lottery Association.

4
00:00:10,508 --> 00:00:15,286
That's one office running the computers that draw the numbers, for lotteries in many states.

5
00:00:15,586 --> 00:00:21,300
See, a lottery computer has one job. It picks numbers nobody can guess, like a robot rolling dice.

6
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:26,357
Now, Eddie was the information security director, so keeping it safe was his job.

7
00:00:26,857 --> 00:00:28,880
Hit like if you see where this is going.

8
00:00:29,180 --> 00:00:31,105
Here's the trick, step by step.

9
00:00:31,405 --> 00:00:34,617
Step one: he later told a court he wrote code into the software.

10
00:00:34,917 --> 00:00:37,372
That code let him predict the winning numbers.

11
00:00:37,872 --> 00:00:41,119
So now it's like knowing the dice roll before anybody throws.

12
00:00:41,419 --> 00:00:44,351
Step two: he said he gave those numbers to other people.

13
00:00:44,651 --> 00:00:47,558
Step three: those people won, and shared the winnings with him.

14
00:00:48,058 --> 00:00:51,372
Send this to your— to whoever in your family still plays every week.

15
00:00:51,672 --> 00:00:56,126
Then came the big one. In twenty ten, a ticket tied to the scheme hit a jackpot.

16
00:00:56,426 --> 00:01:00,015
The prize was advertised at sixteen point five million dollars.

17
00:01:00,515 --> 00:01:04,598
Say you make fifty grand a year. You'd work three hundred thirty years to earn that.

18
00:01:05,098 --> 00:01:09,905
So how much of that jackpot got paid out? Follow, this page decodes the wild ones.

19
00:01:10,405 --> 00:01:12,434
Zero. Nobody ever collected it.

20
00:01:12,934 --> 00:01:16,843
In twenty seventeen, he pleaded guilty, meaning he admitted it in court.

21
00:01:17,343 --> 00:01:20,120
He was sentenced to up to twenty-five years in prison.

22
00:01:20,620 --> 00:01:23,072
So… still trust the lottery? Yes or no.
